WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.360
A former Ukrainian defense minister's call for elections tests how long martial law can suspend normal democratic processes during an active war. This is Omni View, episode 148.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:22.340
Mikhailo Fedorov, who served as defense minister until recently, publicly called for presidential elections to resume despite the ongoing conflict with Russia.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:30.240
Marshal law has been enforced since February 2022, which under Ukrainian law suspends elections for the duration.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.720
The statement comes as the country continues to face Russian attacks and manages its wartime governance.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.980
Fedorov argued that Kiev must restore its democratic process even while the war continues.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:50.320
The call directly challenges the current suspension that has kept president Zelensky in office beyond the original term.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:01:02.200
Ukrainian authorities have maintained that holding national votes while large parts of the country remain under threat would be logistically impossible and potentially unsafe for voters and candidates.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:12.940
Opposition voices, including the former minister, argue that prolonged suspension of elections risks concentrating power without sufficient checks even during conflict.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:25.720
International observers have noted that many democracies have adjusted electoral rules during wars, yet Ukraine's specific constitutional provisions tie the suspension directly to the declaration of Marshal law.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:32.700
The debate centers on balancing security needs against the requirement for periodic renewal of political legitimacy.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:43.180
BBC reporting highlights the legal barrier created by Marshal law, while CNBC coverage focuses on the challenge this poses to Zelensky's wartime authority.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:02:00.400
The strongest argument for resuming elections rests on the principle that democratic legitimacy must be renewed through regular votes, even in wartime, because indefinite suspension of the electoral calendar can erode public trust and allow unchecked executive power to accumulate.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:11.080
Advocates of this view, including former defense minister Fedorov, point to the constitutional requirement that elections resume once the legal trigger of Marshal law is addressed.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:28.740
The strongest argument against immediate elections rests on the practical reality that large areas of territory remain under active threat or occupation, making safe and fair voting impossible without endangering citizens or producing results that lack credibility across divided regions.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:39.520
Officials align with the current government emphasized that the constitution itself provides for this suspension precisely to avoid such risks during declared states of emergency.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:46.660
Parliament or the constitutional court may issue a formal response to the call for elections before the end of the year.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:56.280
Shifting now to Southeast Asia, Thailand welcomed the head of Myanmar's military government for meetings aimed at strengthening ties between the two countries.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:04.180
The visit focused on border security, trade routes and regional stability amid Myanmar's ongoing internal conflict.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:11.860
Thai officials hosted the Myanmar military chief in a move that deepens existing bilateral cooperation on shared concerns.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:18.020
The engagement occurred as Myanmar continues to experience civil strife that affects neighboring states.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:25.980
Thai officials have framed the engagement as necessary for managing shared borders and preventing spillover from Myanmar's civil strife.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:35.400
Regional analysts point out that Thailand has historically maintained pragmatic relations with Myanmar's leadership, regardless of who holds power in Napida.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:44.600
Critics within ASEAN have questioned whether such high-level contact lends legitimacy to the military government at a time when many member states prefer distance.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:53.360
Nikkeh Asia reporting details the stated goals of border management and trade while noting the broader regional context of Myanmar's crisis.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.800
The approach reflects Thailand's long-standing preference for direct engagement over isolation.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.920
Observers will watch for any joint statements on border management or refugee returns in the coming weeks.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:22.700
Moving to developments in African finance, the South African bank Absa reported stronger first half earnings and said it is studying conversion of its Nigeria representative office into a merchant bank while exploring opportunities in Uganda, Zambia, Tanzania and Angola.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:31.760
Net income for the first half reached 12.58 billion rand compared with 11.23 billion rand a year earlier.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:38.100
Chief executive officer Kenny Fila outlined the expansion steps after the earnings release.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:43.720
The moves target markets where the group sees growth potential beyond its South African base.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:52.000
Absa executives have described the moves as part of a deliberate return to a broader African footprint after earlier retrenchment.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:58.700
Local regulators in target countries will ultimately decide whether the proposed structures meet licensing standards.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:07.840
Some African financial analysts note that regional banks face competition from both international players and fast growing local institutions.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:14.900
Bloomberg coverage includes direct comments from the CEO on the strategy and the specific countries under review.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:19.160
The earnings improvement provides the financial headroom for these steps.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.980
The outcome of the Nigeria licensing discussion will indicate how quickly the expansion can proceed.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:39.020
Turning to European industry, Italy's space sector, built around many small and medium-sized firms with specialized engineering skills, is being asked to scale up as European government's increased defense and space spending.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:44.340
The industry remains dominated by these smaller companies despite its niche expertise.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:49.560
European defense planners seek suppliers capable of meeting larger production targets.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.960
The shift comes as overall European space and defense budgets rise.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:03.280
Italian government officials argue that the country's niche expertise can contribute meaningfully to larger European projects if companies combine resources.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:10.740
Industry representatives have warned that forced mergers could erode the very specialization that gives a kalian firms an edge.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:18.460
European defense planners, meanwhile, are seeking fewer but larger suppliers capable of meeting ambitious production targets.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:27.660
Japan Times reporting examines the structural mismatch between Italy's fragmented sector and the scale requirements of current European programs.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:35.140
The tension highlights differing priorities between preserving specialized capabilities and achieving industrial consolidation.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:43.980
Any government-backed consolidation proposals or new joint European contracts involving Italian firms will draw attention in the months ahead.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.000
Now for the economy and technology beat.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:59.880
Japan's major listed firms increased their combined profit forecast for the current fiscal year, projecting a 14% rise driven largely by strong sales in artificial intelligence and chip-related businesses.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.260
The upgrade reflects sustained global demand for advanced components used in data centers and electronics.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:12.940
Several large Japanese groups have benefited from customers diversifying away from other Asian production hubs.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:17.760
Corporate reports tie the improved outlook directly to these technology segments.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:25.120
Corporate reports attribute the upgrade to sustained global demand for advanced components used in data centers and electronics.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:34.400
Some Japanese economists caution that reliance on a narrow set of technology exports leaves earnings vulnerable to shifts in overseas investment cycles.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:41.020
Nike Asia aggregates the company forecasts and highlights the role of AI and semiconductor demand.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:45.020
The revision marks a notable upward adjustment from earlier projections.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:50.080
The next quarterly earnings revisions will show whether the AI-driven momentum continues.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:59.200
In India, firms posted profit increases at the fastest pace in three years, even as global conflicts raised input costs for some sectors.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.620
Company filings show broad-based gains across manufacturing, services and technology exporters.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:10.640
The growth rate marks the strongest performance since the post-pandemic recovery period.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.840
Currency movements and commodity prices remain variables that could affect future results.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:22.600
Analysts at Indian brokerages link the result to steady domestic demand and successful cost management.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:30.180
External observers note that currency movements and commodity prices remain variables that could affect the next reporting period.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:37.440
Nike Asia summarizes the earnings trends and notes the resilience despite external shocks from ongoing conflicts.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:42.900
The outcome demonstrates that domestic factors can offset some international pressures.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:47.260
The upcoming quarterly results will reveal whether the growth rate holds.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.120
Now, some progress worth knowing about.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:56.740
LG Energy Solution has begun operations at a new battery manufacturing facility in the United States,

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.020
that will supply cells to both Toyota and Tesla.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:08.500
The plant adds domestic production capacity for electric vehicle batteries at a time when US automakers are scaling up electric models.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:13.740
The investment responds directly to customer requirements for localized supply chains.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:20.480
US trade policy continues to favor North American battery production through tax credits and content rules.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:26.740
The company has described the investment as a direct response to customer requirements for localized supply.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:35.520
US industry participants acknowledge that building and qualifying new plants at this scale remains technically demanding and capital intensive.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.180
Nike Asia reports on the facility opening and its specific customers.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:45.120
The development adds concrete manufacturing capacity in a key growth sector.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:50.180
Production volumes from the new site will be tracked against announced targets for the coming year.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:55.260
Now, to really understand this story, there is something most coverage leaves out.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:10:00.060
Most coverage assumes elections are simply postponed by practical difficulties.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:08.320
Yet Ukraine's constitution contains an explicit clause that ties the suspension of national votes directly to the legal state of martial law.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:20.120
Under that framework, the president and parliament remain in office until the law is lifted, creating a built-in mechanism that prevents scheduled elections without needing separate legislation each time.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:30.240
The same rules have been applied in earlier periods of conflict, showing that the current arrangement follows an established constitutional path rather than an ad hoc decision.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:41.240
Because the clause is automatic, any move to restore elections requires either ending martial law or amending the constitution, both of which carry their own procedural thresholds.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:49.440
Knowing this distinction helps readers separate logistical arguments from the legal trigger that actually keeps the electoral calendar frozen.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:57.100
When officials or critics discuss holding elections during war, the key test is whether they are addressing the constitutional bar

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.400
or only the security and organizational obstacles.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:11.420
Readers can check the text of Ukraine's martial law statute and the relevant constitutional articles to see exactly which provisions are active and what would be required to lift them.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:24.780
The mechanism also means that lifting martial law would automatically reopen the electoral timeline, shifting the focus from security logistics alone to the broader political decision of ending the emergency declaration.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:35.440
Historical application during prior conflicts demonstrates that the suspension has operated as a standard constitutional response rather than a unique wartime exception.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:45.500
If you want to go deeper on the Ukrainian elections debate, compare how BBC and CNBC are covering it. You will see two different frames on the same facts.

